# Changelog

## 1.2.0 - 2026-08-10

### Fixed

- `stickyel` and `shyel` measured once and never again. Anything that reflows the
  page — a rotated phone, a collapsed banner, a webfont arriving, a header that
  shrinks as you scroll — left the element pinning at a position that no longer
  existed, or hiding by the wrong amount. Both now re-measure on resize.
- Teardown removed the scroll listener but left any run already queued, so a
  handler could still touch an element the caller had finished with. Teardown now
  cancels the pending run as well.

### Changed

- Scroll handlers are coalesced to one run per animation frame instead of on a
  20ms/50ms timer. The work now lands immediately before the paint that shows it,
  rather than at an arbitrary point in the frame where the browser has to redo
  layout it had already settled.
- **Removed the lodash dependency.** It was pulled in as CommonJS, so bundlers
  could not tree-shake it and consumers shipped roughly 72KB minified for two
  functions. The package now has no third-party runtime dependencies.

### Added

- `wrap` on `scrollClass`, `shyel` and `stickyel`, for callers who want their own
  rate-limiting instead of the per-frame default — lodash's `throttle` and
  `debounce` already have the right shape. If the returned handler has a `cancel`
  method, teardown calls it.
- `onFrame`, the default wrapper, exported for direct use, with the
  `IScrollOptions`, `IScrollHandlerWrapper` and `IWrappedScrollHandler` types.

## 1.1.0 - 2026-08-10

### Fixed

- `types` pointed at `types/index.d.ts`, which the build never produces — it
  emits declarations to `dist/types/`. Published versions up to 1.0.5 therefore
  ship no usable types at all. The dead `types` entry in `files` and the
  `rm -rf ./types` in the publish script are gone with it.
- `prepublish` runs on `npm install`, not on publish, so a plain install of this
  repo ran the full build, browser suite and docs build — and failed. Renamed to
  `prepublishOnly`, with the checks themselves under `npm run verify`.
- `scrollClass` threw a `TypeError` when given an `HTMLCollection`, which its own
  signature accepts and which `getElementsByClassName` and `.children` return.
- `setIntersection` debounced the IntersectionObserver callback by 10ms. Debounce
  keeps only the last invocation, so any batch of entries delivered less than
  10ms before another was silently discarded and those elements were never
  reported. The debounce is removed; the observer already batches its own work.
- `setIntersection` ignored `single: true` unless an `intersectingCallback` was
  also supplied.
- `applyLazyPicture` listened for `load` on the `<picture>` element. Only the
  inner `<img>` loads and its `load` event does not bubble, so the loaded class
  was never applied. The listener now sits on the `<img>`.
- `activateIntersection`, `activateIntersectionOnce` and `activateLazyload` had
  their parameter types inferred from their `querySelectorAll` defaults, which
  rejected the plain arrays that every function they delegate to accepts.
- `activateIntersectionOnce` never stopped observing. The class it applies is
  never removed, so every revealed element stayed under observation for the life
  of the document. It now unobserves an element once it has actually activated —
  and only then, so a mobile-only element declined on a wide viewport can still
  activate if the viewport narrows.
- The placeholder prefix accepted by `setLazyAttributes` could not be reached
  through `applyLazyImage`, `applyLazyPicture`, `applyLazyVideo`, `setLazyload`
  or `activateLazyload`. All five now take it and pass it down.
- `globals` was a runtime dependency; it is only used by the eslint config.
- `license` was `AGPLv3.0`, which is not a valid SPDX identifier.

### Added

- Unit, property-based and type-level test suites on vitest + jsdom, covering
  all twelve runtime exports and the three exported interfaces.
- A packaging smoke test that packs the tarball, installs it into a clean
  project and imports it as both ESM and CJS.
- Mutation testing with per-file score floors in `mutation-baseline.json`.

### Changed

- The lazy helpers gained a trailing optional `prefix` argument and the three
  `activate*` helpers accept arrays as well as NodeLists. Both are additive: no
  existing call changes meaning.
- `npm test` runs the unit suite; `npm run cy:test` runs the browser suite with
  its fixture server.
- The browser suite is reliable and no longer skips anything. Two specs were
  asserting on impossible geometry: `Custom marginRoot` used a -400px margin on
  a 660px viewport, which leaves no band at all, and both of its scroll
  positions put a target edge exactly on the band boundary. The
  `activateIntersectionOnce` spec expected a target that is only ever fully
  visible part-way through an animated scroll. The viewport is now pinned in
  `cypress.config.ts`, since the specs assert against real geometry.
- The lazyload specs ran only in the interactive runner, so headless they
  registered nothing and the spec was still counted as passing. They now run
  everywhere, against local fixtures instead of remote hosts, one of which no
  longer exists.
- `npm run verify` is the single gate, wired to the pre-commit hook and to
  `prepublishOnly`. The hook is activated by the `prepare` script, which the
  repository declared through the long-removed husky v4 config block and so had
  never run.
- Removed `cy:kill`, a Windows-only `TASKKILL /IM node.exe /F` that killed every
  node process on the machine. `cy:test` starts and stops its own server.
